  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a large family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that there&amp;nbsp;is an identified need, would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers, and would not be located in an area with a high level of access to public transport. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&amp;nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&amp;nbsp;Policies&amp;nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&amp;nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)-&amp;nbsp;Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&amp;nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate&amp;nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;especially as the application site is located within the HW Controlled Parking Zone (CPZ), where on‑street parking demand is already managed through restrictions. The proposal is therefore likely to&amp;nbsp;exacerbate existing parking stress within the CPZ thus&amp;nbsp;add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&amp;nbsp;which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&amp;nbsp;Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&amp;nbsp;Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
